  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;GOLDEN PASS PIPELINE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; page-break-after: avoid; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;NOTES TO FINANCIAL STATEMENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 24pt; page-break-after: avoid; border-bottom: 0.75pt solid #000000; padding-bottom: 1pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;AS OF AND FOR THE YEARS ENDED DECEMBER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;31, 2025 AND 2024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 18.26pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid; padding-left: 4.24pt; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;ORGANIZATION AND BUSINESS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Golden Pass Pipeline&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;LLC (&amp;#8220;GPPL&amp;#8221; or the &amp;#8220;Company&amp;#8221;) is a Delaware limited liability company owned 70% by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;QatarEnergy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt; U.S. Investments (1) LLC (&amp;#8220;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;QatarEnergy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8221;) and 30% Golden Pass Pipeline Investments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;LLC (&amp;#8220;GPPL Investments&amp;#8221;) (collectively, the &amp;#8220;Members&amp;#8221;). The Company operates under the provisions provided in the Limited Liability Company Agreement executed by the Members and is subject to the jurisdiction of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company is affiliated with Golden Pass LNG Terminal LLC (&amp;#8220;GPLNG&amp;#8221;) through common shareholder ownership. GPLNG is a Delaware registered limited liability company owned 70% by &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;QatarEnergy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt; and 30% by Golden Pass LNG Terminal Investments LLC (&amp;#8220;GPLNG Investments&amp;#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Both GPPL Investments and GPLNG Investments are affiliates of Exxon Mobil Corporation. Since July 1, 2025, GPLNG has been the anchor shipper on Company&amp;#8217;s pipeline and has contracted 100% of its available capacity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company owns and operates a 70&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;mile interstate natural gas transmission system (the &amp;#8220;Golden Pass Pipeline&amp;#8221;) that provides transportation of natural gas under pro forma firm or interruptible contracts to various receipt and delivery points along its system. GPPL connects to multiple interstate and intrastate pipelines capable of either delivering or receiving natural gas, and is equipped with two compressor stations located at Milepost 33 (&amp;#8220;MP33&amp;#8221;) and Milepost 69 (&amp;#8220;MP69&amp;#8221;) that were placed into service on December 1, 2025. The Golden Pass Pipeline is considered &amp;#8220;bi-directional&amp;#8221; as it can transport gas in a northward direction as well as in a southward direction. The Company has extensive operations and relationships with the Members as well as GPLNG and other related parties. See Note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;8 of these financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company placed its pipeline into service in 2011. Effective 2010, the Company entered into three long-term firm transportation agreements (&amp;#8220;FTAs&amp;#8221;) with ConocoPhillips Company, ExxonMobil LNG Supply&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;LLC, and GPLNG (collectively, the &amp;#8220;Shippers&amp;#8221;) for 100% of the pipeline capacity. The Shippers have continued to make monthly capacity reservation payments since the &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;pipeline in-service date in 2011 until termination of the three agreements on July 1, 2025. These agreements were initially executed for a term of twenty-five&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;years. In 2019, the Shippers amended their agreements to terminate early to coincide with the then-expected export project commercial operational date (&amp;#8220;COD&amp;#8221;) of GPLNG&amp;#8217;s Train 1. The agreements terminated on July 1, 2025, and GPLNG was awarded its bid to the full pipeline capacity for a term of approximately five (5) months until the compression project was completed (the &amp;#8220;Interim Contract&amp;#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; color: #ff0000;"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Upon placing the compression facilities into service on December 1, 2025, GPLNG, the Company&amp;#8217;s anchor shipper, began its new long-term firm agreement for a term of 25-years to be followed by two optional 10-year extensions for a total possible term of 45-years. Coinciding with placing the compression facilities into service, GPPL also put into effect its revised FERC Gas Tariff including a new maximum recourse reservation rate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Certain GPLNG facilities (the &amp;#8220;Sabine Spur Facilities&amp;#8221;) located adjacent to GPPL interconnect with Natural Gas Pipeline Company of America at Milepost 01 (&amp;#8220;MP01&amp;#8221;) and connecting to the GPLNG Terminal were constructed by the Golden Pass Pipeline project team on behalf of GPLNG. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;See Note 3 for further discussion of the current ratemaking process and status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="2" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 13.76pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid; padding-left: 8.74pt; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Prior period adjustment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Display';"&gt;The Company identified an inadvertent miscalculation of depreciation rates for the period December 1, 2023 through December 31,2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The correction of the depreciation rate for the Company's FERC reporting results in a cumulative adjustment of FERC retained earnings of approximately $3.6 million, as of December 31, 2025 approved by FERC Docket AC26-27-000, as summarized in the table below (in millions):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 632.25pt; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr style="height: 46.7pt;"&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 324.6pt; padding: 0.5pt 5.9pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;Line Item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 68.25pt; padding: 0.5pt 5.9pt; vertical-align: bottom;"&gt;
