&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;(3.6)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 19.75pt; padding: 0.5pt 5.9pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="width: 80.2pt; padding: 0.5pt 5.9pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Aptos Narrow';"&gt; 678.3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;The accompanying financial statements of GPPL have been prepared in accordance with the accounting regulations of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;#8220;FERC&amp;#8221;), as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which are a comprehensive basis of accounting other than generally accepted accounting principles (&amp;#8220;GAAP&amp;#8221;) in the United States. The most significant difference between GAAP and the comprehensive basis of accounting applied in these Financial Statements is the classification of certain accounts on the Comparative Balance Sheet, Statement of Income and Statement of Cash Flows. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;The preparation of financial statements in conformity with&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;accounting requirements of the FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;requires management to make certain estimates and assumptions that affect the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;amounts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;reported in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;the Financial Statements and the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;accompanying notes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Management evaluates its estimates and related assumptions regularly, including those related to useful lives of net utility plant , recognition of asset retirement obligations (&amp;#8220;AROs&amp;#8221;) as further discussed under the respective sections within this note. Changes in facts and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;circumstances or additional information may result in revised estimates, and actual&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;results&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;may&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;differ from these estimates.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Accounts Receivable from Associated Companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;Balance primarily relates to unbilled reserved capacity revenue under the firm transportation agreement with GPLNG. See Note 8 &amp;#8211; Transactions with Associated Companies for more details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Plant Materials and Operating Supplies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;Balance primarily consists of materials and supplies, carried at the lower of cost or net realizable value and subsequently charged to operating expenses and maintenance expenses at average cost when issued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Operational Imbalances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;The Comparative Balance Sheet includes natural gas imbalance receivables and payables resulting from quantities of gas confirmed and scheduled by the parties to be delivered to or received from the contractually defined location (the &amp;#8220;Location&amp;#8221;) that may be greater or lesser than the quantities of gas which are actually delivered or received at the Location, resulting in over- or under-deliveries or receipts relative to the scheduled quantities. Under the operational balance agreements (&amp;#8220;OBAs&amp;#8221;), volumes owed to or by GPPL are typically settled in-kind within the following month and valued based on contractual terms and regulatory jurisdictional requirements. Operational imbalances subject to cash settlement are valued in accordance with the contractual requirements of the respective OBAs. Operational imbalances are reported in Account 174, Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Assets and Account 242, Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities in the Comparative Balance Sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Net Utility Plant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;Net utility plant is recorded at cost. Expenditures for construction activities, major renewals and betterments that extend the useful life of an asset or enhance functionalities and safety are capitalized, while expenditures for maintenance and repairs (including major overhaul projects) to maintain net utility plant in operating condition are generally expensed as incurred. Excluding land, which is not depreciated, utility plant is depreciated using the straight&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;line method. The depreciation rate for the Transmission Plant assets is 2% as approved by the FERC. Generally, upon retirement or other disposition of net utility plant, the cost and related accumulated depreciation are removed from their respective accounts, and the resulting difference after the consideration of any proceeds and any costs to remove, sell or dispose of the assets are recorded in Accounts 108, 111, 115, Accumulated Provision for Depreciation, Amortization and Depletion. If a retirement constitutes an extraordinary property loss by approval or order of the Commission, Account 182, Extraordinary Property Loss is charged. Gains or losses on retirements of gas plant are not recognized on the Statement of Income unless the asset is for land or gas plant constituting an operating unit or system (as approved by the FERC).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Management tests net utility plant for impairment whenever events or changes in circumstances have indicated that the carrying amount of net utility plant might not be recoverable. Assets are grouped at the lowest level for which there are identifiable cash flows that are largely independent of the cash flows of other groups of assets for purposes of assessing recoverability. Recoverability generally is determined by comparing the carrying value of the asset to the expected undiscounted future cash flows of the asset. If the carrying value of the asset is not recoverable, the amount of impairment loss is measured as the excess, if any, of the carrying value of the asset over its estimated fair value. The Company did not record any material impairments related to net utility plant and equipment for the years ended December 31, 2025, and 2024.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Allowance for Funds Used During Construction (&amp;#8220;AFUDC&amp;#8221;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;AFUDC represents the capitalized carrying cost of capital funds related to the construction of long-lived assets and is depreciated over future periods as part of the total cost of the related asset. The rates used in the calculation of AFUDC are determined in accordance with guidelines established by the FERC. Under regulatory rate practices, the Company generally is permitted to recover AFUDC, and a fair return thereon, through its rate base.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Asset Retirement Obligations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;The Company recognizes AROs for legal obligations associated with the retirement of long&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;lived assets that result from the acquisition, construction, development or normal use of the asset and for conditional AROs in which the timing or method of settlement are conditional on a future event that may or may not be within our control. The fair value of a liability for an ARO is recognized in the period incurred, if a reasonable estimate of fair value can be made. The fair value of the liability is added to the carrying amount of the associated asset. This additional carrying amount is depreciated over the estimated useful life of the asset.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company is subject to regulations by the FERC for proper abandonment of a pipeline, including the disconnection of the pipeline from all sources and supplies of gas and other decommissioning costs. The Company believes that it is not feasible to predict when the pipeline will no longer be utilized. In addition, right&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;of&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;way agreements associated with the pipeline have no stipulated termination dates. The Company intends to operate the pipeline as long as supply and demand for natural gas exists in the United States and intends to maintain it in accordance with all applicable laws and regulations. For these reasons, GPPL has not recorded an ARO associated with the pipeline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 14pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;GPPL has FTAs with its shippers. For the years 2024 through the first half of 2025, GPPL had three FTAs with Shippers. Beginning July 1, 2025, GPLNG is the only FTA shipper on GPPL and holds 100% of the pipeline capacity. Revenue from FTAs is based on capacity reservation fees. Revenue is recognized over time, using an output method based on time as each service period expires to measure complete satisfaction of the single series performance obligation. At December 31, 2025, the FTA has a remaining term of up to 45 years. GPLNG has continuous access to its firm transportation capacity during the contract term but has no ability to defer unused capacity to future months. Under this arrangement, GPLNG pays fixed fees of $8.8 million per month, totaling $105.8 million per year, to reserve the right to transport natural gas up to a maximum contractually specified level of 2,600,910 dekatherms per day ("&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Dth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;/d"), regardless of the quantities that GPLNG actually transports.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;GPPL may also enter into arrangements to provide transportation services to additional customers on a fee per-unit rate for the quantities actually transported. Such services are generally described as interruptible services, which GPPL stands ready to provide to the customer, however the customer accepts the possibility that service may be interrupted at GPPL&amp;#8217;s discretion in order to provide services under reserved capacities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Fair Value Measurements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;Fair value is the price that would be received to sell an asset or paid to transfer a liability in an orderly transaction between market participants. The carrying amount of cash and cash equivalents, third-party accounts receivable, accounts payable and accrued liabilities reported on the Balance Sheets approximates fair value due to their short&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;term nature.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Concentration of Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;Financial instruments that potentially subject the Company to a concentration of credit risk consist principally of cash and accounts receivable. The Company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;maintains cash balances at financial institutions, which may at times be in excess of federally insured levels. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company has not incurred losses related to these balances to date. The Company has entered into a long-term FTA for which it is dependent on the counterparty&amp;#8217;s creditworthiness and its willingness to perform under the agreement. The Company has mitigated this credit risk by securing the agreement with a creditworthy customer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Subsequent Events&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#8212;The Company has performed an evaluation of subsequent events through April 9&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;, 2026, the date the financial statements were available to be issued.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="3" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 13.76pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid; padding-left: 7.84pt; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;&lt;span style="-aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;REGULATORY MATTERS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;The Company is a &amp;#8220;natural gas company&amp;#8221; as defined by the NGA, 15 U.S.C. Sections 717&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Cambria Math';"&gt;&amp;#8209;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;717W and is subject to the jurisdiction of the FERC. The transportation of natural gas in interstate commerce is provided in accordance with a Certificate of Public Convenience and Necessity issued to the Company by FERC under section 7(c) of the NGA; Part 157, Subparts A &amp;amp; F and Part 284, Subpart G of the Commission Regulations (18 CFR Parts 153, 157 and 284).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;In 2019, the Company filed a Stipulation and Agreement (&amp;#8220;Settlement&amp;#8221;) and pro forma tariff records pursuant to rules 207(a)(5) and 602 of the FERC&amp;#8217;s regulations to implement a total rate reduction of approximately 46% to GPPL&amp;#8217;s maximum base tariff rate for Rate Schedules Firm Transportation (&amp;#8220;FT&amp;#8221;) and Interruptible Transportation (&amp;#8220;IT&amp;#8221;). The Settlement filed by the Company was approved and made effective July 1, 2019, and terminated after the agreed-upon moratorium period on July 1, 2025.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;On January 29, 2025, FERC approved the Company&amp;#8217;s application for a new pro forma tariff that offers additional transportation services along with a significant number of other general changes to bring the new tariff in line with others in the industry. For the period from July 1, 2025 (the termination of the prior FTAs) to December 1, 2025 (the effective date of GPLNG&amp;#8217;s new FTA for 100% of the pipeline&amp;#8217;s capacity) GPLNG held an FTA for the full capacity of GPPL with a term of five-months. Upon placing the compression facilities into service on December 1, 2025, GPLNG began its new firm agreement for a term of 25-years with two optional 10-year extensions. Coinciding with placing the compression facilities into service, GPPL also put into effect a new maximum recourse reservation rate.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 21.6pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; font-size: 11pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Calibri;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol style="margin: 0pt; padding-left: 0pt;" start="4" type="1"&gt;
&lt;li style="margin-left: 14.01pt; margin-bottom: 9pt; page-break-after: avoid; padding-left: 7.59pt; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase;"&gt;NET UTILITY PLANT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
