    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HHB707D481BFCE62FCEF04F10BCA283E7C" xlink:to="HHCBFECBA828FA13C84A63F15A7F5CF7C9" order="1" />
    <link:loc xlink:type="locator" xlink:href="#HH296A4D66DEBE3BDAADB0B0C7FAC9E70B" xlink:label="HH296A4D66DEBE3BDAADB0B0C7FAC9E70B" />
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="HH7EB2954293969678B7DE26FBBA304911" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote" xml:lang="en">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>The Company receives certain administrative and general services from GPLNG for project team management, staffing, facilities, and related support. In 2024, the costs of services were charged using estimates based on a methodology in accordance with the services agreements between the Company and GPLNG. Effective January 1, 2025, GPLNG and GPPL memorialized the intercompany charge-out process by entering into a formal agreement, whereby GPLNG charges GPPL an annual fee of $11.0 million, adjusted annually for inflation, to cover shared services for certain support functions and reimbursement for administrative and general costs incurred on behalf of GPPL, billed in monthly installments. Direct charges incurred by GPPL are excluded from the agreement, such as those incurred in connection with capital or operating costs like pipeline maintenance and salaries for dedicated employees. Amounts charged by GPLNG for these services under the agreements were $11.0 million and $11.6 million in 2025 and 2024, respectively, included in the Statements of Operations.&#160;</p>
        <p>&#160;</p>
        <p>The Company utilizes third party services, staffing, facilities, and related support for the construction of the Sabine Spur Facilities. The capital expenditures have been charged using methods in accordance with the construction services agreements between the Company and GPLNG. Amounts charged (credited) to GPLNG for these services were $(3.6) million and $25.3 million in 2025 and 2024, respectively. On October 1, 2025, the Company entered into an operations and maintenance agreement with GPLNG to operate and maintain the Sabine Spur Facilities on behalf of GPLNG. No amounts were incurred in 2025 under this agreement, as the facilities have not commenced operations.&#160;</p>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnoteArc xlink:type="arc" xlink:arcrole="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/arcrole/fact-footnote" xlink:from="HH296A4D66DEBE3BDAADB0B0C7FAC9E70B" xlink:to="HH7EB2954293969678B7DE26FBBA304911" order="1" />
